settings-niri-backdrop-card = Niri
settings-niri-backdrop-card-desc = Keep a separate backdrop, or use one stationary wallpaper that blurs only in overview.
settings-niri-show-label = Show wallpaper in overview
settings-niri-show-desc = Keep a separate backdrop, or use one stationary wallpaper that blurs only in overview.
settings-niri-blur-static-label = Blur images
settings-niri-blur-static-desc = Blur image backdrops once when they load. This costs almost nothing while the overview is open.
settings-niri-blur-static-radius-label = Image blur radius
settings-niri-blur-static-radius-desc = Blur radius for image backdrops, from 0 to 100. Higher is softer.
settings-niri-blur-video-label = Blur videos
settings-niri-blur-video-desc = Blur every video frame while the overview is open. This uses noticeably more GPU than a sharp video, especially at 4K.
settings-niri-blur-video-radius-label = Video blur radius
settings-niri-blur-video-radius-desc = Blur radius for video backdrops, from 0 to 100. Higher is softer.
settings-niri-blur-we-label = Blur Wallpaper Engine scenes
settings-niri-blur-we-desc = Blur every scene frame while the overview is open. This uses noticeably more GPU than a sharp scene.
settings-niri-blur-we-radius-label = Wallpaper Engine blur radius
settings-niri-blur-we-radius-desc = Blur radius for Wallpaper Engine backdrops, from 0 to 100. Higher is softer.
settings-niri-follow-label = Always use the current wallpaper
settings-niri-follow-desc = Follow the wallpaper you apply. Turn off to choose a separate backdrop below.
settings-niri-image-label = Backdrop source
settings-niri-image-desc = Choose Set as backdrop on a wallpaper, or enter an image, video, or Wallpaper Engine project path. Leave empty to use the last wallpaper.
settings-niri-auto-theme-label = Auto-theme the backdrop
settings-niri-auto-theme-desc = Recolour static images with a gowall theme palette. Videos and Wallpaper Engine scenes keep their original colours.
settings-niri-theme-label = Backdrop theme
settings-niri-theme-desc = Palette used when auto-theming the backdrop.
settings-niri-dim-label = Backdrop dimming
settings-niri-dim-desc = Darken the overview backdrop. 0 = none, 100 = black.
settings-niri-rule-label = Required niri layer-rule
settings-niri-rule-desc = Add the layer rules to ~/.config/niri/config.kdl. Merge the layout and overview settings into existing blocks.
settings-niri-refresh-label = Refresh backdrop now
settings-niri-refresh-desc = Reload the selected source with the current blur, dimming, and theme settings.
settings-niri-refresh-action = Refresh
settings-niri-copy-label = Copy layer-rule to clipboard
settings-niri-copy-desc = Copies the snippet above for niri's config.
settings-niri-copy-action = Copy

settings-niri-mode-label = Overview mode
settings-niri-mode-desc = Keep a separate backdrop, or use one stationary wallpaper that blurs only in overview.
settings-niri-mode-separate = Separate backdrop
settings-niri-mode-stationary = Stationary wallpaper
settings-niri-stationary-desc = Uses the current wallpaper and the default video renderer. Add the Niri configuration below. Blur and dimming apply only in overview.
